;W[qf]C[Wariuchi at 13 is better. The 12 and 37 become miai. The sequence up to 25 leaves black with a better position. ]
;B[qi];W[qc];B[qd];W[pc];B[od];W[rd];B[re];W[rc];B[qe];W[nc];B[nd];W[mc];B[le];W[qo]
C[This move is rather poor - white only creates a heavy, weak group. A play directly at 30 would be more appropriate.]
;B[ro];W[qn];B[pq];W[pj];B[pl]C[Better at 32.];W[qj];B[rl];W[ri];B[nk];W[rk]C[White has given up three stones in exchange for the security of the group including 30.  The overall result is better for white, although black now has sente.]
;B[ql];W[ph];B[cl];W[fc];B[dc];W[md];B[me];W[of];B[nf];W[kd];B[ni];W[sl]C[With this move white is certain of life.]
;B[sm];W[sk];B[rn];W[ci];B[ef]C[Although large in relation to the corner and the upper side, this move is not urgent. Black should have played at 54 to leave white with a weak group.]
;W[el];B[em];W[fm];B[en];W[dl];B[cm];W[co];B[cn];W[ep];B[bo];W[bp];B[do];W[cp];B[fp]
;W[fo];B[fn];W[go];B[gm];W[fl];B[gn];W[ck]C[54-74\: In attacking black's group, white formed territory on the lower side and secured eye-shape for the left side group. Moreover, he still has some aggressive potential.]
;B[ho];W[gp];B[in];W[jp];B[ko];W[mo]C[This was the sealed move, Played quickly, it is an obvious mistake since white cannot afford to answer 85 at 87. White 80 at 87 would have been about 10 points better. ]
;B[hp];W[hq];B[iq];W[gq];B[lp];W[kq];B[mp];W[hk]C[White thought that he was losing and played 88 to reduce black's centre, but 89 was very severe. If white had played 88 at 90, then he would still have been ahead.]
;B[ic];W[hd];B[oc];W[ob];B[id];W[ie];B[he]C[Fatal mistake. After this white can play 96, force black to escape, and then capture 95 to gain easy life to the left. 95 should be at 97, and then black can either escape without giving white eyes, or, should white block the exit to the centre, connect underneath 40. ]
