;W[bg]C[Poor yose. This should be at 114 to keep sente. The sequence played lft white in gote, and enabled black to take the initiative in the centre with 117.]
;B[bf];W[jj];B[kj];W[bh];B[rg];W[qh];B[ij];W[ji];B[ik];W[ki];B[kb];W[ok];B[nl];W[dg]
;B[df];W[ch];B[cf];W[af];B[ae];W[ag];B[bb]C[117-131\: Both players have been striving to gain on the centre-left. The sitution is now fairly conclusive in this area and attention turns to the right, where white tries to take advantage of the weakness at 138.]
;W[lj];B[kk];W[lk];B[ll];W[kc];B[jb];W[lg]C[This move hits the vital point of black's formation.]
;B[lf];W[nh]C[White cannot play directly at 149 because there are too many cutting points.]
;B[mi];W[gb]C[Black should make eyes for his group by playing 141 and 143.];B[mg]
